            <ArticleTitle>Intracardiac tumor: an unusual case of myocardial ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have presented an unusual case of right ventricular tumor mimicking myocardial ischemia. Tumor invasion of deeper structures of the heart is rare, and we think the ECG and enzyme changes in our patient were due to invasion of the ventricular septum by the tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
